{% comment %}
  Shorelines through time: average shoreline per decade (tools/hatteras_decadal_shorelines.py) over a choice of
  NC OneMap aerial photos. Script: assets/hatteras/js/decadal-shorelines.js. The page needs `map: true`.
{% endcomment %}
<div class="hat-shoremap hat-bleed hat-decadal" id="decadal" data-src="{{ '/assets/hatteras/data/decadal_shorelines.json' | relative_url }}">
  <div class="hat-shoremap-inner">
    <div class="hat-controls">
      <div class="hat-seg" role="group" aria-label="Aerial photo underneath" id="decadal-photos">
        <button type="button" data-photo="latest" class="on">Latest photo</button>
        <button type="button" data-photo="1993">1993</button>
        <button type="button" data-photo="2002">2002</button>
        <button type="button" data-photo="2016">2016</button>
        <button type="button" data-photo="2024">2024</button>
      </div>
      <div class="hat-seg" role="group" aria-label="Zoom to a place">
        <button type="button" data-goto="35.245,-75.525,14">Cape Point</button>
        <button type="button" data-goto="35.262,-75.518,15">Buxton</button>
        <button type="button" data-goto="35.346,-75.502,15">Avon</button>
        <button type="button" data-goto="35.590,-75.463,15">Rodanthe</button>
        <button type="button" data-goto="35.695,-75.485,14">Pea Island</button>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="hat-mvo-arms" id="decadal-years" aria-label="Shorelines shown"></div>
    <div class="hat-decadal-wrap">
      <div id="decadal-map" role="region" aria-label="Map of the average shoreline in each decade since the 1980s"></div>
      <div class="hat-decadal-loading" aria-hidden="true">Loading photo…</div>
    </div>
    <p class="hat-caption hat-numbered">
      The average shoreline in five-year windows centred on 1985, 1995, 2005, 2015 and 2025, from every satellite shoreline
      in each window (the last window ends with the record in January 2026). Each line joins the average position on the
      survey lines, 50 m apart; a gap means too few clear images. Satellite shorelines mark the water's edge at mean sea level,
      so they sit on the wet beach in the photos, not at the dunes.
      Photos: NC OneMap / NC Center for Geographic Information and Analysis; latest photo with USGS The National Map at island scale.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>
<script defer src="{{ '/assets/hatteras/js/decadal-shorelines.js' | relative_url }}"></script>
